<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anwar Sadat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1981</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anwar Sadat was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from 1970 until his assassination in 1981. He launched the October War of 1973 against Israel, opened the economy and turned Egypt from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> towards the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. He signed the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords and the peace treaty of 1979 with Israel, for which he shared the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-peace-prize">Nobel Peace Prize</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat.jpg" alt="Anwar Sadat" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anwar_Sadat_cropped_(cropped)(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
